Modifier types of the host's own (Segno, modulators: docs/design/modulators.md §17).

tracktion knows six modifier types, named in four places; a host can't add its own. Segno's
modulators are modifiers of their own types, so:
- ModifierList::isCustomType and createCustom let the host name and make its own types. They're
  then modifiers everywhere tracktion asks (isModifier), their assignments are automation sources
  (isAutomationSourceType, also on load), and adding or removing one rebuilds playback (the Edit's
  tree watcher), undo and redo included.
- Modifier::getValueFor asks a modifier for the value one assignment sees at an edit time. The
  default is what tracktion did (the current value, or the history's for a time behind it); a
  modulator overrides it to give each target its own copy (Per Target) and values exact to the
  time between block starts.
- ProcessingPosition::beforePlugin with getPluginToProcessBefore() processes a modifier at its
  place in the track's chain (just before that plugin), so a follower hears the sound there.
  Without that plugin in the chain, it's processed after the chain.

